    "concept": {
      "variant_id": "B5-v002",
      "brief_id": "B5",
      "direction": "monolith_slab",
      "name": "Monolith Slab \u2014 Chamfered Top-Intake Air-Quality Detector",
      "form_language": "A single unbroken plan-view rectangle with a continuous 3 mm 45\u00b0 chamfer running the full perimeter of both the front face and the back face, so the part reads as a machined slab rather than a moulded box. The front face is a quiet, uninterrupted field: no raised bezel, no parting-line step, no visible fastener. The parting line is placed on the 3 mm chamfer band itself and is masked from paint, so the chamfer becomes the only intentional line in the design. The top face carries the full air path \u2014 a recessed intake grille band sunk 1.2 mm below the top surface so it never reads as a bump, with a matching exhaust slot on the bottom face (not called out here) to give a straight vertical airflow chimney over the sensor. The only interruption to the front field is a flush, slightly recessed display window (0.6 mm below the painted surface) framed by the chamfer's shadow line. Volume is a constant-thickness slab: front and back faces are parallel planes, all slimness is expressed at the silhouette edge, not by tapering.",
      "silhouette": "chamfered_slab",
      "envelope_mm": {
        "length": 125.0,
        "width": 75.0,
        "height": 26.0
      },
      "corner_radius_mm": 6.0,
      "display": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 56.0
      },
      "display_window_mm": {
        "width": 78.0,
        "height": 34.0
      },
      "intake": {
        "face": "top",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 50.0
      },
      "usb": {
        "face": "right",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 50.0
      },
      "cmf": {
        "material": "rABS",
        "finish": "smooth_matte",
        "color": "Warm Graphite Grey, matte, L*\u224838, low specular sheen (soft-touch lacquer over rABS, \u0394E \u2264 1.5 batch-to-batch)",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "soft_touch",
          "laser_etch",
          "pad_print"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "The perimeter 3 mm 45\u00b0 chamfer is the parting line and the only visible seam; it must remain uncoated (masked) for the full 360\u00b0 so the ultrasonic weld / gasket land is never painted.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Front face stays a flat, uninterrupted painted plane with the display window recessed 0.6 mm; no raised bezel, no bosses, no visible screws or parting-line step on the front.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Intake is a single recessed grille band on the top face, sunk 1.2 mm, centred at x=50 / y=50, backed by an ePTFE membrane over a gasket land \u2014 this is the IP67 air path and must not be moved to the front or side faces.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Housing is 100% rABS with a masked soft-touch matte lacquer on exterior visible surfaces only; wall stock held at 1.5 mm nominal to keep the mass budget inside the 151 g relaxed cap.",
          "category": "sustainability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "USB-C is on the right face on the vertical centreline, sealed by a captive silicone flap; the right face is the only face allowed a functional cut-out other than the top intake.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Decorating is restricted to laser-etch and pad-print (no secondary painted graphics, no IML) to stay inside the relaxed CNY 16 ceiling at 10,000 units/year.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The chamfered_slab direction is chosen because it is the cheapest reliable way to deliver the brief's 'premium + slim + waterproof' triple under the relaxed constraints. A slab with parallel faces needs no compound-curve tooling, so rABS can run in a simple two-plate tool with a single straight-pull chamfer \u2014 this protects the CNY 16 ceiling and the six-week design-freeze window far better than a pebble or capsule form. Putting the parting line on the 3 mm chamfer solves Q2 directly: the chamfer band is masked before paint, giving the gasket and ultrasonic weld a clean, paint-free land while every visible face still gets the soft-touch matte lacquer. Placing the intake on the top face (rather than the front) does three things at once \u2014 it keeps the front a clean display plane for the aesthetics priority, it creates a natural vertical chimney through the sensor for airflow, and it lets the intake be a shallow 1.2 mm recess that does not break the silhouette or add a proud grille that could snag. The ePTFE membrane over that recessed band is the R-vent resolution and is the single biggest IP67 cost item, so it is deliberately concentrated in one small top-face area instead of being spread across front perforations. The 6 mm plan-view corner radius and 45\u00b0 edge chamfer are sized to survive handling drops without a sharp edge, and the 1.5 mm wall keeps the part inside the relaxed 151 g mass cap with the 92 g internal stack. rABS plus masked soft-touch lacquer plus laser-etch/pad-print is the lowest-cost route to a premium tactile surface that also satisfies the 100% recycled-plastic must-have."
    },
